{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "text": "%md\n# INF2006 G12 — Task 3: Next-week stock price direction (FINAL candidate notebook)\nThis notebook is **self-contained**: load the existing Task 2 S3 tables, create past-only features, compare a few models, choose the probability cutoff using 2016 validation data, evaluate on 2017 test data once, save the final pipeline and verify reloading.\n\n**How to run:** Import this `.zpln` into Zeppelin, then click **Run all** or run the cells in order. download numpy : **sudo python3 -m pip install numpy**\n\n**Meaning of class 1:** the stock closes higher after the next five trading sessions. In both notebooks, the model predicts a **class**, not an exact future price or numerical volatility. The probability score estimates the likelihood of class 1.\n\n**Important:** Only use information from the current or earlier date as a feature. The test split is for the final one-time assessment, not repeated tuning.\n",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-11-14T18:25:57+0000",
