        "msg": [
          {
            "type": "HTML",
            "data": "<h1>INF2006 G12 — Task 3: Next-week stock price direction (FINAL candidate notebook)</h1>\n<p>This notebook is <strong>self-contained</strong>: load the existing Task 2 S3 tables, create past-only features, compare a few models, choose the probability cutoff using 2016 validation data, evaluate on 2017 test data once, save the final pipeline and verify reloading.</p>\n<p><strong>How to run:</strong> Import this <code>.zpln</code> into Zeppelin, then click <strong>Run all</strong> or run the cells in order. download numpy : <strong>sudo python3 -m pip install numpy</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Meaning of class 1:</strong> the stock closes higher after the next five trading sessions. In both notebooks, the model predicts a <strong>class</strong>, not an exact future price or numerical volatility. The probability score estimates the likelihood of class 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> Only use information from the current or earlier date as a feature. The test split is for the final one-time assessment, not repeated tuning.</p>\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "text": "%spark.pyspark\n# CELL 1 — Settings and tools.\n# The bucket/path come from your successful V1 Direction notebook.\nimport time, json, datetime\nfrom pyspark.sql import functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\nfrom pyspark.ml import Pipeline, PipelineModel\nfrom pyspark.ml.feature import Imputer, VectorAssembler, StandardScaler\nfrom pyspark.ml.classification import LogisticRegression, GBTClassifier\nfrom pyspark.ml.evaluation import BinaryClassificationEvaluator\nfrom pyspark.ml.functions import vector_to_array\n\nspark.conf.set(\"spark.sql.shuffle.partitions\", \"32\")\nBUCKET = \"inf2006-g12-ml\"\nBASE = \"s3a://\" + BUCKET\nINPUT = BASE + \"/task2/model_ready_v1\"\nPRICES_PATH = BASE + \"/task2/cleaned/cleaned/prices\"\nRUN_ID = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\")\nOUT = BASE + \"/task3/final_models/direction_v2/\" + RUN_ID\nSEED = 42\nSPLITS = [\"training\", \"validation\", \"testing\"]\nBASE_FEATURES = [\"daily_return\", \"return_5d\", \"volatility_20d\", \"volume_change_1d\", \"intraday_range\"]\n# These came from V1, which you already tested.\nEXTRA_V1 = [\"volatility_5d\", \"volatility_60d\", \"vol_ratio_5_60\", \"abs_return_5d\",\n            \"range_5d\", \"return_20d\", \"volume_z_20d\", \"market_return_1d\", \"market_volatility_5d\"]\n# These are new: longer-term trends, relative strength, and market breadth.\nNEW_FEATURES = [\"return_10d\", \"return_60d\", \"price_to_ma20\", \"price_to_ma60\",\n                \"price_in_range_20d\", \"return_vs_vol20\", \"relative_return_5d\",\n                \"relative_return_20d\", \"market_avg_return_5d\", \"market_avg_return_20d\",\n                \"market_breadth_1d\", \"market_breadth_5d\"]\nTREND_FEATURES = BASE_FEATURES + [\"return_10d\", \"return_20d\", \"return_60d\",\n             \"price_to_ma20\", \"price_to_ma60\", \"price_in_range_20d\", \"return_vs_vol20\", \"volatility_5d\"]\nMARKET_FEATURES = TREND_FEATURES + [\"market_return_1d\", \"market_avg_return_5d\",\n                   \"market_avg_return_20d\", \"market_breadth_1d\", \"market_breadth_5d\",\n                   \"relative_return_5d\", \"relative_return_20d\"]\nFULL_FEATURES = list(dict.fromkeys(BASE_FEATURES + EXTRA_V1 + NEW_FEATURES))\nprint(\"Direction V2 | Spark\", spark.version, \"| RUN_ID\", RUN_ID)\nprint(\"Input\", INPUT)\nprint(\"Output\", OUT)\n",
      "user": "anonymous",
